From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:51:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Find and list the databases of a storage bottle in
 the client storage registry

The client storage registry knows every IndexedDB database in storage:
each has a row in `databases` (bottle, name) with its directory in
`directories`. Until now it could only create (or look up while creating)
and delete one, so the IndexedDB manager had no way to find a database it
hadn't opened itself, such as one from an earlier session.

Add two read-only registry operations, in both registry engines (SQLite
and the RDB twin) with the same SQL:

- FindDatabase / ClientStorageThreadHandle::find_database: the directory
  of the database `name` in a bottle, if it exists.
- ListDatabases / ClientStorageThreadHandle::list_databases: the databases
  of a bottle with their directories, in creation order.

Names are stored as text, or, for a name with an unpaired surrogate, as a
BLOB of its UTF-16 code units (RegistryDatabaseName). The list reads both
forms back, by `typeof(name)`: RDB fails to read the size of a NULL that a
CASE expression gives, so the two forms can't be two columns. A BLOB that
holds no name is skipped with a warning. Later commits use these for
deleteDatabase, open and databases().

The handle's requests don't unwrap their send: a message that the client
storage thread can't take any more is dropped with its reply sender, so
the receiver reports the disconnection instead of the asking thread
panicking, such as the IndexedDB manager's client storage calls at
shutdown (P5 review N4).

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 152 passed, 1 skipped (new tests/client_storage.rs test_find_and_list_databases: two bottles, a BLOB name, a deleted database); DAYU200 unit tests: client_storage_ohos_rdb.rs test_ohos_registry_finds_and_lists_databases passes with RDB only and with both backends (a first version that read the two name forms from two CASE columns failed there with OH_Cursor_GetSize 14800000); `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets` with SQLite, RDB and both: no warnings; after the P5 review fix: 154 passed, 1 skipped at this commit, with the new test_requests_after_exit_fail (the handle's requests after the client storage thread exited report the disconnection; it panics with the old unwraps)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote the registry operations for both engines and their tests; the P5 review fix removed the unwraps, with its test)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
